According to AIS-004, Clause 5.1, the relevant vehicle electrical/electronic systems or ESAs are those which are involved in immunity related functions of the vehicle, such as functions related to the direct control of the vehicle, including: 

(i) engine, gear, brake, suspension, active steering, speed limitation devices; 
(ii) systems affecting driver's position, such as seat or steering wheel positioning; 
(iii) systems affecting driver's visibility, such as dipped beam, windscreen wiper. 

These systems are considered relevant for immunity related functions as they are involved in the direct control of the vehicle or affect the driver's ability to control the vehicle.

According to AIS-004, Clause 5.1, the immunity related functions of the vehicle include functions related to the direct control of the vehicle, such as: 
(i) by degradation or change in: e.g. engine, gear, brake, suspension, active steering, speed limitation devices; 
(ii) by affecting driver’s position: e.g. seat or steering wheel positioning; 
(iii) by affecting driver's visibility: e.g. dipped beam, windscreen wiper.
